@page "/docs/components/input-time"
@page "/docs/components/time-picker"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.InputTime
<PageTitle>Input Time - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Input Time</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="input-time" />
        </div>
        <p>An inline time field bound to a <code>TimeOnly</code>, with hour, minute and optional seconds segments that you type into or step in place. <code>HourCycle</code> picks the clock: the browser's locale by default, or a forced 12 or 24-hour layout. Pair it with <a href="/docs/components/calendar">Calendar</a> for a date and time picker.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(InputTimeBasicExample)"
                Description="Import `Blaizio.Ui` once, then bind a nullable `TimeOnly` to `Value` two-way." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Basic" Description="An hour and minute field with a leading clock icon. Whether it shows a 12 or 24-hour clock follows the browser's locale."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeBasicExample)" />

    <Demo Title="12- and 24-hour" Description="`HourCycle` forces the clock regardless of the browser locale. `TwelveHour` adds an AM/PM toggle you can click, step with the arrows or set with A and P, while `TwentyFourHour` shows hours from 00 to 23. Typing digits moves focus to the next segment on its own."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeHourCycleExample)" />

    <Demo Title="With seconds" Description="`ShowSeconds` adds a seconds segment, and the native step becomes one second."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeSecondsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Minute step" Description="`MinuteStep` sets how far the arrow keys move the minutes. Here each press jumps 15 minutes."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeStepExample)" />

    <Demo Title="No icon" Description="Set `ShowIcon` to `false` for a bare field without the clock, or pass `Icon` to use your own glyph."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeNoIconExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Programmatic focus" Description="Keep a reference to the component and call `FocusAsync` to move focus from code. Here a shortcut sets the time and returns focus to the field. With an explicit `HourCycle` focus goes to the first segment, while on `Auto` it lands on the browser's own time input."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeFocusMethodExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Description="`Disabled` grays out the field and blocks editing."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Classes passed through `Class` merge over the field defaults, which covers width, radius and a brand focus ring. The `Icon` slot swaps the leading glyph."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeCustomExample)" />

    <Demo Title="RTL"
          Description="Inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, the field mirrors and the clock icon moves to the inline-end edge, while the hour and minute digits keep their normal order."
          Example="typeof(InputTimeRtlExample)" />

</div>

